Title: No Wind
Author: Hugh Howey

EXT. LEEVILLE MARINA - NIGHT

Fog sits on the bayou like it was poured there. Shrimp boats nod against their fenders, rigging slack.

Out past the channel markers, a bell buoy rings. Slow. Even. Patient.

There is no wind.

INT. HARBOR OFFICE - CONTINUOUS

Tide charts on every wall. A VHF radio hisses on the desk. VERNON LIRETTE (70s), suspenders over an undershirt gone gray, stands at the window with a cold cup of coffee.

The door bangs open. KIM BROUSSARD (40s) shoulders in, wetsuit peeled to the waist, hair still dripping.

KIM
That's three nights.

VERNON
(not turning)
Four. You slept through Sunday.

KIM
There's no buoy on the chart out there, Vernon.

She drops a coil of chain on his desk. Rust-black, heavy, still streaming water. The last link has been cut clean through.

The cut shines like a new dime.

KIM
Somebody anchored it. And somebody came back for it.

Vernon sets the coffee down. He looks at the chain for a long time.

VERNON
Fuel up the Louella.

CUT TO:

EXT. MISS LOUELLA - NIGHT

The trawler noses through the fog, running lights haloed. Kim at the bow with a spotlight. Vernon at the wheel.

The bell. Close now.

KIM
There.

The beam finds it. A buoy, all right. Old iron, crusted with barnacles, rocking on dead-flat water.

Rocking.

VERNON
Leave it. We go home.

KIM
(quiet)
We should call somebody. The Coast Guard. Shana's brother still runs the station at Grand Isle, doesn't he? He'd come out. He owes you for the thing with the outboard, and you know he does, and you know he'd come out tonight if you called him instead of standing there like the fog is going to answer for you.

VERNON
He'd laugh at us.

KIM
He'd laugh at you.

Vernon throttles down. The engine ticks. The buoy keeps rocking.

Under the bell, faint, something else. A voice. Counting.

VERNON
You hear that?

KIM
I hear it.

INT. MISS LOUELLA - WHEELHOUSE - CONTINUOUS

Vernon grabs the radio handset. Static. He twists the dial. Static.

VERNON
Leeville harbor, this is the Miss Louella. Anybody up?

Static. Then, under it, the counting again. Closer.

KIM (O.S.)
Vernon!

EXT. MISS LOUELLA - BOW - CONTINUOUS

Kim leans over the rail with the spotlight. In the water, just under the surface, a second chain. It runs straight down. Taut.

Something below is holding the buoy still. Something below is making it rock.

KIM
It's not anchored. It's tethered.

VERNON (O.S.)
To what?

She doesn't answer. She's already pulling on her mask.

EXT. GULF - UNDERWATER - CONTINUOUS

Dark. Bubbles. Kim's light cuts a narrow tunnel through silt.

The chain descends. Ten feet. Twenty. At thirty she stops.

A second buoy. Upside down. Hanging below the first, its bell swinging in the black water. Ringing.

There is no current down here either.

SMASH CUT TO:

INT. HARBOR OFFICE - DAWN

Gray light. Vernon asleep in his chair. The chain still on the desk. The cut link is gone.
